WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.100
Julia was so terrified she could hardly breathe. Still, she didn't hesitate.

2
00:00:09.101 --> 00:00:17.188
"Stop!" she cried, leaping away from the time passage. "It's not Markos' fault. We'll stay."

3
00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:24.416
She glanced at Brody, but he appeared to be frozen in place. Julia couldn't believe it.

4
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:30.208
Was he thinking about stepping through the passage despite Hermes' threats against Markos and his family?

5
00:00:30.209 --> 00:00:37.407
A second later she let out a sigh of relief as Brody stepped away from the passage too.

6
00:00:37.408 --> 00:00:41.985
"It's cool," he said. "I didn't really want to go anyway.

7
00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:45.802
I was totally looking forward to being in the Olympics."

8
00:00:45.803 --> 00:00:52.708
"You have a funny way of showing it, boy," Hermes snarled, though he sounded slightly less angry already.

9
00:00:52.709 --> 00:00:57.253
"Come. We need to have a talk about loyalty." As

10
00:00:57.254 --> 00:01:02.322
Hermes dragged Brody out of the room, Julia glanced at Markos. He'd

11
00:01:02.323 --> 00:01:06.494
taken a few steps forward and was staring through the passage. Julia

12
00:01:06.495 --> 00:01:12.030
glanced through at her own world just in time to see a car drive by. "Oh!"

13
00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:17.615
Markos exclaimed, pointing at it. "What was that?" "It's

14
00:01:17.616 --> 00:01:25.354
a car," Julia said. "It's like a wagon, except you don't need a horse or ox to pull it." Markos

15
00:01:25.355 --> 00:01:27.949
looked impressed. "Never

16
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:31.806
mind. Let's step away from the time passage, shall we?" Caerus

17
